< {"citation":{"abstract":"MicroRhodoDB curates Type-I microbial rhodopsin proteins from UniProtKB with explicit, evidence-graded membership decisions (member/candidate status vocabulary), QC features, redundancy handling, a phylogenetically placed reference tree (MR_RT_003, ~472 tips) with 19 named subfamilies, a five-level function evidence ladder (E1-E5) backed by literature-verified assertions, a frozen post-cutoff external validation set, and an isolated environmental (MGnify) pilot layer kept separate from the core, evidence- graded corpus. Version 1.6.0 adds function-call conflict flags (conflicting E3/E4 calls downgraded), an expanded E1 set with labelled publication links, engineered-construct flags, a curated membership override for 4 experimentally characterised E1 proteins, a blind audit of E2-E4 calls, a family-HMM flag and Foldseek watchlist for novel families, a full data dictionary and a static browser with in-browser sequence search. Releases are immutable, versioned SQLite databases; the current release is rebuilt from the previous one by a pinned Snakemake workflow.","authors":[{"family-names":"Li","given-names":"CongJian"}],"date-released":"2026-10-09","doi":null,"license":"CC-BY-4.0","message":"If you use MicroRhodoDB, please cite it using the metadata in this file. A companion data-descriptor manuscript is in preparation for submission to Database (Oxford) or Scientific Data; this file will be updated with the paper citation once it is published.","repository-code":"https://github.com/CongjianL/MicroRhodoDB","title":"MicroRhodoDB: a versioned, evidence-aware knowledgebase of Type-I microbial rhodopsins","type":"dataset","version":"1.6.0"},"citation_source":"CITATION.cff","dataset_release":"1.6.0","maintenance_placeholders":[{"context":"Contact address: [not supplied]","hint":"institutional e-mail","status":"not supplied (pending confirmation by the maintainer)"},{"context":"Corpus updates: [not supplied]","hint":"e.g. one release per year, foll